WEBVTT

00:01.007 --> 00:03.377
<b>I've gathered
the biggest, burliest men around</b>

00:03.467 --> 00:06.347
<b>and paying them to carry my mikoshi
and serve as my bodyguards.</b>

00:06.427 --> 00:09.557
<b>And I shall shoot them all
from right here,</b>

00:09.637 --> 00:12.097
<b>in the safety of my own little box.</b>

00:12.177 --> 00:17.607
<b>This is my very own battle mikoshi plan!</b>

00:18.517 --> 00:19.817
<b>It's all for show.</b>

00:19.897 --> 00:22.777
<b>That huge thing
will just become an easy target.</b>

00:22.857 --> 00:24.817
<b>No, not necessarily.</b>

00:25.777 --> 00:28.447
<b>It's so conspicuous
that it's bound to become a target, but…</b>

00:29.447 --> 00:31.697
<b>The bearers wear heavy armor</b>

00:31.787 --> 00:33.767
<b>and maintain a tight formation
around the poles.</b>

00:33.577 --> 00:34.577
<b>RAMPAGE! BATTLE MIKOSHI</b>

00:34.387 --> 00:37.247
<b>They can't be taken down easily,
even in close combat.</b>

00:38.087 --> 00:41.877
<b>Even if one bearer falls,
another one immediately takes his place.</b>

00:44.127 --> 00:45.717
<b>Even if they reach the mikoshi…</b>

00:55.767 --> 00:58.517
<b>This is bad.
They're packing in tighter and tighter.</b>

00:58.607 --> 00:59.607
<b>PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL</b>

00:59.267 --> 01:02.607
<b>If they pack in that tightly,
Sadamune's army will slip in behind them.</b>

01:02.437 --> 01:03.547
<b>SADAMUNE'S ARMY
HOSHINA PARTY</b>

01:03.567 --> 01:05.447
<b>They could be cut off and wiped out.</b>

01:06.277 --> 01:08.697
<b>Fubuki? Don't be reckless!</b>

01:08.777 --> 01:11.867
<b>No need to worry. I'm going
as a messenger to pass on my idea.</b>

01:13.747 --> 01:16.117
<b><i>That's the danger of a court noble
who knows nothing of war.</i></b>

01:16.207 --> 01:18.457
<b><i>Tactics that defy
a warrior's expectations can be</i></b>

01:18.537 --> 01:19.957
<b><i>extremely dangerous
if they happen to work.</i></b>

01:22.627 --> 01:27.177
<b>Trample them to death! Cut them down!</b>

01:27.257 --> 01:30.407
<b>I'll shoot them down too!</b>

01:30.427 --> 01:32.927
<b>All for my world…</b>

01:36.017 --> 01:40.557
<b>No, for the Emperor's world.</b>

01:41.227 --> 01:44.227
<b><i>It's beyond me.</i></b>

01:44.317 --> 01:46.357
<b><i>I could never govern those beasts</i></b>

01:46.357 --> 01:49.697
<b><i>who wouldn't hesitate
to take a Provincial Official's life.</i></b>

01:50.617 --> 01:52.327
<b><i>Even if it's my command?</i></b>

01:54.077 --> 01:57.327
<b><i>Our Kiyohara clan has always been
a lower-ranked noble house.</i></b>

01:57.407 --> 02:00.827
<b><i>We have neither the lineage nor the
worthiness to become Provincial Officials.</i></b>

02:01.627 --> 02:03.717
<b><i>Why did you appoint someone like me</i></b>

02:03.717 --> 02:06.717
<b><i>as a Provincial Official
in the first place?</i></b>

02:08.217 --> 02:12.847
<b><i>Kiyohara,
lineage is not what I value most.</i></b>

02:13.967 --> 02:15.177
<b><i>It is resolve.</i></b>

02:15.267 --> 02:18.637
<b><i>I value those with
the resolve to change the age.</i></b>

02:19.767 --> 02:23.477
<b><i>Even in the days of Kamakura,
you must have wondered.</i></b>

02:24.227 --> 02:26.277
<b><i>"Why do indolent court nobles</i></b>

02:26.857 --> 02:30.407
<b><i>who fawn over
the shogunate's warrior families</i></b>

02:30.487 --> 02:33.617
<b><i>and cling to their privileges
still hold power?"</i></b>

02:34.827 --> 02:39.157
<b><i>"I could change the world
if I were in their place."</i></b>

02:40.207 --> 02:43.997
<b><i>I saw the passion, ambition,
and resolve hidden in your eyes.</i></b>

02:44.707 --> 02:47.547
<b><i>I recognized your worth even then.</i></b>

02:49.507 --> 02:54.757
<b><i>You had noticed a mere
minor court noble like me even back then?</i></b>

02:56.137 --> 02:58.057
<b><i>Your house has no standing.</i></b>

02:58.137 --> 03:00.637
<b><i>You have no achievements
on the grand stage.</i></b>

03:00.727 --> 03:03.807
<b><i>Yet you possess a resolve
that reaches the heavens.</i></b>

03:03.897 --> 03:05.647
<b><i>That is why I entrust Shinano to you.</i></b>

03:06.817 --> 03:08.277
<b><i>Go, Kiyohara.</i></b>

03:08.857 --> 03:13.697
<b><i>Rule Shinano with that resolve,
for the world I shall create.</i></b>

03:14.617 --> 03:16.987
<b><i>The Emperor commands you to go!</i></b>

03:17.617 --> 03:18.827
<b><i>Yes, sir!</i></b>

03:20.537 --> 03:22.747
<b><i>Emperor Godaigo was also a hero</i></b>

03:22.827 --> 03:26.207
<b><i>possessed of unparalleled charisma
and force of character.</i></b>

03:27.087 --> 03:29.507
<b><i>As though imbued
with the Emperor's own spirit,</i></b>

03:29.587 --> 03:34.137
<b><i>many nobles took up unfamiliar weapons
and risked their lives on the battlefield.</i></b>

03:35.427 --> 03:38.217
<b><i>It was one of the most unusual
characteristics of the era.</i></b>

03:39.387 --> 03:42.807
<b>Mr. Hoshina,
move your soldiers to the left.</b>

03:44.187 --> 03:47.067
<b>Concentrate as many soldiers as you can
from the right to the left.</b>

03:49.477 --> 03:52.447
<b>All for the Emperor's reign!</b>

03:53.027 --> 03:58.367
<b>We shall build his world here in Shinano!</b>

04:16.637 --> 04:21.477
<b>THE ELUSIVE SAMURAI</b>

05:29.537 --> 05:30.997
<b>Heave-ho!</b>

05:31.087 --> 05:32.207
<b>Heave-ho!</b>

05:35.507 --> 05:37.507
<b>Cry out, you fools.</b>

05:37.587 --> 05:40.967
<b>Your voices are the bells
that herald the new reign.</b>

05:41.637 --> 05:46.307
<b>To build a righteous world,
we must first cut away its impurities.</b>

05:46.807 --> 05:51.057
<b>The Emperor's reign shall bloom
upon that blood.</b>

06:00.277 --> 06:03.117
<b>Emperor, behold!</b>

06:03.197 --> 06:07.997
<b>That blood is
the very proof of my loyalty.</b>

06:09.667 --> 06:12.207
<b>I've concentrated the troops
as you instructed, but…</b>

06:12.287 --> 06:14.047
<b>Fire!</b>

06:14.127 --> 06:16.257
<b>There are too many of them.</b>

06:16.337 --> 06:17.667
<b>No matter how many we cut down,</b>

06:17.757 --> 06:20.427
<b>it's as if they just keep crawling out
from the depths of the earth.</b>

06:20.507 --> 06:22.677
<b>Don't worry. Keep it up.</b>

06:25.017 --> 06:27.597
<b>It should be about time.</b>

06:32.647 --> 06:35.067
<b>What's going on? Hold it steady!</b>

06:36.317 --> 06:38.987
<b>Damn it!
Where are the replacement bearers?</b>

06:47.867 --> 06:51.877
<b>What are you dawdling for?
Get back into formation!</b>

06:52.997 --> 06:55.587
<b>Not many can wield a sword
with their left hand.</b>

06:56.637 --> 07:00.677
<b>If we strike there,
we can break the bearers' formation.</b>

07:01.177 --> 07:02.637
<b>The left!</b>

07:02.717 --> 07:04.757
<b>Concentrate your attacks from the left!</b>

07:05.387 --> 07:08.307
<b>Follow me, Shinomiya!
We're taking the enemy commander!</b>

07:10.057 --> 07:14.307
<b>It's shaking! It's shaking!
At this rate, I can't use my bow!</b>

07:31.957 --> 07:32.957
<b>It's over.</b>

07:33.747 --> 07:35.837
<b>In the end, it was just
a court noble's little game.</b>

07:37.247 --> 07:39.667
<b>Let's get back and collect our reward.</b>

07:39.757 --> 07:42.217
<b>After all,
we took down that Provincial Official.</b>

07:42.297 --> 07:44.507
<b>Don't make it sound like it was all you!</b>

07:44.597 --> 07:46.007
<b>Huh? Wasn't it?</b>

07:49.677 --> 07:50.977
<b>What's wrong, brat?</b>

07:51.977 --> 07:52.977
<b>Well…</b>

07:54.267 --> 07:56.567
<b>The mountain behind Shinomiya's main army…</b>

07:57.437 --> 07:58.437
<b>Just now, something…</b>

08:01.607 --> 08:02.607
<b><i>A glint…</i></b>

08:06.027 --> 08:07.407
<b><i>Arms?</i></b>

08:12.037 --> 08:13.037
<b>The mountain?</b>

08:15.247 --> 08:16.287
<b>My lord?</b>

08:17.667 --> 08:20.087
<b>We need to ready
Shinomiya's army to retreat!</b>

08:20.167 --> 08:22.877
<b>At worst, they'll be ambushed from behind!</b>

08:22.967 --> 08:26.177
<b>Huh? That's impossible.</b>

08:25.007 --> 08:26.177
<b>SHINOMIYA'S MAIN ARMY</b>

08:26.257 --> 08:29.347
<b>Behind the Shinomiya's army
is nothing but endless mountains.</b>

08:29.427 --> 08:32.727
<b>There's no way an army that large
could get in there…</b>

08:36.227 --> 08:40.777
<b>Besides, my lord, the enemy's
main commanders should all be out by now.</b>

08:45.657 --> 08:47.737
<b><i>There's one man who comes to mind.</i></b>

08:50.197 --> 08:56.417
<b><i>A cunning, meticulous commander
known for mountain ambushes.</i></b>

08:56.917 --> 08:58.207
<b>SHINOMIYA'S MAIN ARMY</b>

08:57.197 --> 08:59.797
<b>An ambush from the mountain behind us?</b>

09:03.417 --> 09:04.837
<b>There's no sign of anything.</b>

09:06.467 --> 09:08.257
<b>What's your basis for that?</b>

09:08.347 --> 09:11.767
<b>I have none,
but please order a retreat at once!</b>

09:11.847 --> 09:14.517
<b>We've beaten the Provincial Official
and we're on the verge of victory.</b>

09:14.597 --> 09:16.557
<b>We can't move the main army now.</b>

09:19.107 --> 09:21.437
<b>In our land, where we revere the divine,</b>

09:21.527 --> 09:23.937
<b>the idea of a man
riding a mikoshi is absurd.</b>

09:24.027 --> 09:26.067
<b>Only a god
has the right to ride a mikoshi.</b>

09:26.147 --> 09:28.947
<b>And in Shinano, there's only one.</b>

09:32.657 --> 09:35.287
<b>We'll hear you out
once Lord Shinomiya returns.</b>

09:35.827 --> 09:38.377
<b>By then, it'll be too late.
It's the instinct of a born runner.</b>

09:38.457 --> 09:39.667
<b>Please, hurry!</b>

09:39.747 --> 09:40.747
<b>E…</b>

09:41.417 --> 09:43.877
<b>Enemy… Enemy…</b>

09:44.757 --> 09:45.757
<b>Enemy?</b>

09:51.507 --> 09:54.677
<b>Enemy attack!</b>

09:54.767 --> 09:55.767
<b>What's happening?</b>

09:58.267 --> 09:59.267
<b>Yasaburo!</b>

09:59.347 --> 10:00.357
<b>Damn it!</b>

10:03.527 --> 10:06.897
<b>I'll go after him!
Shinomiya, get back to the main army!</b>

10:13.907 --> 10:15.577
<b>Run for it!</b>

10:17.787 --> 10:18.787
<b>Young Lord!</b>

10:19.287 --> 10:21.077
<b>Kojiro! Genba!</b>

10:40.647 --> 10:41.897
<b><i>Shokan…</i></b>

10:56.077 --> 10:57.117
<b>Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

11:06.667 --> 11:07.797
<b>SOUTH - CENTER - NORTH</b>

11:06.667 --> 11:09.467
<b>The battle began on three fronts.</b>

11:09.547 --> 11:13.097
<b>Within days, the northern and
southern forces would be consolidated,</b>

11:13.177 --> 11:17.467
<b>and both sides would converge
on the center for the decisive battle.</b>

11:18.637 --> 11:21.397
<b>After analyzing both armies' strength,</b>

11:21.477 --> 11:23.767
<b>I predicted the decisive battle
on the fourth day</b>

11:23.857 --> 11:26.777
<b>and moved my troops
through the mountains accordingly.</b>

11:27.527 --> 11:30.567
<b>Then I learned of
the Provincial Official's secret weapon</b>

11:30.647 --> 11:32.607
<b>and worked it into my plan.</b>

11:32.697 --> 11:37.037
<b>It was the perfect toy to draw
everyone's attention on the battlefield.</b>

11:37.117 --> 11:40.077
<b>While everyone's attention
was focused on the mikoshi,</b>

11:41.367 --> 11:45.787
<b>we swiftly closed in on Shinomiya's main
camp and launched a surprise attack.</b>

11:48.087 --> 11:51.217
<b>This is military strategy, Chojumaru.</b>

11:52.547 --> 11:53.547
<b>Military strategy…</b>

11:55.597 --> 11:58.597
<b>You may run around
hunting down petty commanders</b>

11:58.677 --> 12:00.847
<b>and save small villages.</b>

12:01.517 --> 12:04.187
<b>But if you can't read
the tide of a great war,</b>

12:04.267 --> 12:08.527
<b>you'll never attain anything truly great.</b>

12:09.607 --> 12:14.027
<b>You should've had
Kusunoki teach you the art of war.</b>

12:14.567 --> 12:18.117
<b>But what a shame.
Good children, it's time to die!</b>

12:18.197 --> 12:19.197
<b>Young Lord!</b>

12:20.037 --> 12:22.957
<b>They're on foot.
They can't catch us on horseback.</b>

12:24.117 --> 12:25.127
<b>Right.</b>

12:27.127 --> 12:29.297
<b>Impressive, Shokan.</b>

12:29.797 --> 12:32.627
<b>Your plan worked perfectly.</b>

12:33.467 --> 12:34.467
<b>Lord Sadamune.</b>

12:35.927 --> 12:39.007
<b>I took the opportunity to break through
their defensive line.</b>

12:39.717 --> 12:43.017
<b>Now we'll wipe out Shinomiya's army
in one sweep!</b>

12:43.097 --> 12:44.347
<b>As you command!</b>

12:46.647 --> 12:52.487
<b><i>A single move by one commander overturned
the entire course of the battle.</i></b>

12:53.737 --> 12:54.857
<b><i>This is war.</i></b>

12:56.237 --> 12:57.907
<b><i>This is military strategy.</i></b>

12:58.907 --> 13:02.447
<b>Damn it!
While I was away from the main army…</b>

13:03.327 --> 13:07.127
<b><i>No… Once an army has fallen apart,
it can't be reformed.</i></b>

13:07.207 --> 13:08.207
<b>Mr. Shinomiya!</b>

13:09.167 --> 13:10.417
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

13:10.497 --> 13:12.877
<b>If only I'd realized it sooner…</b>

13:13.547 --> 13:15.217
<b>Don't be ridiculous.</b>

13:15.297 --> 13:18.297
<b>If warriors have to rely on a child
that much, we're no warriors at all.</b>

13:19.097 --> 13:22.977
<b>Right now, I'm thinking about
how to salvage this defeat.</b>

13:23.557 --> 13:28.477
<b>Just like Hoshina,
we can't simply abandon our land.</b>

13:29.307 --> 13:33.737
<b>But if we stand our ground in this chaos,
total annihilation is inevitable.</b>

13:43.407 --> 13:45.327
<b>Mr. Mochizuki?</b>

13:46.537 --> 13:50.337
<b>Sorry. He blew up our own men too,
so please rescue them.</b>

13:50.837 --> 13:51.957
<b>Yeah…</b>

13:52.547 --> 13:54.417
<b>As one of
the Three Great Generals of the Suwa Sect,</b>

13:54.507 --> 13:56.377
<b>I have a message for the Shinomiya party.</b>

13:57.177 --> 14:00.217
<b>Remember this.
In this battle, fleeing is victory.</b>

14:00.717 --> 14:02.967
<b>We'll serve as the rear guard
and buy you time.</b>

14:03.057 --> 14:06.227
<b>Take your clan
and withdraw to Hoshina territory.</b>

14:07.137 --> 14:13.647
<b>Suwa Myojin will surely rise.
Live on and await that day.</b>

14:17.697 --> 14:18.987
<b>Suwa Myojin…</b>

14:19.067 --> 14:20.277
<b>How reassuring.</b>

14:20.367 --> 14:23.577
<b>For that day,
we'll endure any humiliation.</b>

14:24.827 --> 14:26.287
<b><i>What a relief.</i></b>

14:26.367 --> 14:29.747
<b><i>Words from one of the Three Great Generals
carry a different kind of weight.</i></b>

14:30.327 --> 14:33.497
<b>All right.
We'll leave the enemy to Lord Mochizuki.</b>

14:33.587 --> 14:35.207
<b>Prepare to withdraw!</b>

14:35.297 --> 14:36.627
<b>Yeah!</b>

14:37.757 --> 14:40.507
<b>Mr. Mochizuki,
weren't you supposed to be in the north?</b>

14:40.587 --> 14:42.637
<b>Why are you here?</b>

14:42.717 --> 14:47.477
<b>After that, I went to tell Father
about the battle in the center.</b>

14:47.557 --> 14:53.727
<b>The moment he heard my report, he said,
"How boring," and left right away.</b>

14:53.817 --> 14:54.817
<b>"Boring"?</b>

14:54.897 --> 14:56.147
<b>Yeah.</b>

14:56.237 --> 14:59.857
<b>The enemy's movements here
were too boring.</b>

15:00.527 --> 15:03.527
<b>So I had a feeling
there'd be an interesting twist,</b>

15:03.617 --> 15:05.287
<b>and that worried me.</b>

15:05.367 --> 15:08.117
<b>That's so random… but I'm glad he came.</b>

15:09.207 --> 15:12.037
<b>This battle was never likely to be won.</b>

15:12.537 --> 15:16.417
<b>Lord Yorishige still can't act openly,
so it was unavoidable.</b>

15:17.757 --> 15:19.877
<b>Both the Inukai and Tokoiwa clans
had been told</b>

15:19.967 --> 15:23.467
<b>to hide in the mountains if defeated.</b>

15:23.547 --> 15:27.387
<b>Lord Yorishige had already prepared
supplies and shelter for them.</b>

15:28.767 --> 15:30.597
<b>This is merely a preliminary battle.</b>

15:31.137 --> 15:32.977
<b>Lord Yorishige's objective
is to keep casualties to a minimum</b>

15:33.057 --> 15:37.317
<b>and strengthen the unity of the Suwa Sect.</b>

15:38.567 --> 15:41.067
<b><i>Mr. Yorishige had even
calculated that far ahead…</i></b>

15:41.777 --> 15:45.117
<b><i>A profound military strategy of
a kind completely different from Shokan's.</i></b>

15:45.867 --> 15:46.907
<b>And, Young Lord.</b>

15:48.197 --> 15:49.787
<b>Your selfless devotion,</b>

15:49.867 --> 15:53.497
<b>running day and night
and risking your life for the Suwa Sect,</b>

15:54.037 --> 15:57.667
<b>has deeply moved us all.</b>

15:59.207 --> 16:00.417
<b>When the next great war comes,</b>

16:00.507 --> 16:05.927
<b>we, the people of Shinano, pledge that
we will spare no effort in supporting you.</b>

16:10.097 --> 16:12.727
<b><i>Our final mission as the Elusive Warriors</i></b>

16:12.807 --> 16:16.397
<b><i>was to carry word of the defeat on
the Central Front to the Southern Front.</i></b>

16:17.727 --> 16:19.147
<b><i>The moment they received the message,</i></b>

16:19.227 --> 16:22.237
<b><i>Mr. Unno and Mr. Nezu
rushed to the Central Front.</i></b>

16:23.607 --> 16:25.527
<b><i>Thanks to
the Three Great Generals' valiant stand,</i></b>

16:25.617 --> 16:27.987
<b><i>the Shinomiya party was rescued
from the brink of destruction,</i></b>

16:28.077 --> 16:30.697
<b><i>and casualties were kept to a minimum.</i></b>

16:31.747 --> 16:32.957
<b><i>With all hope of victory lost,</i></b>

16:33.037 --> 16:35.667
<b><i>Mr. Tokoiwa in the north
and Mr. Inukai in the south</i></b>

16:35.747 --> 16:37.167
<b><i>fled into the mountains.</i></b>

16:37.917 --> 16:41.587
<b><i>Kiyohara, the Provincial Official,
escaped in the confusion.</i></b>

16:43.297 --> 16:46.467
<b><i>We barely managed to hold back
Shokan and Ogasawara's army,</i></b>

16:46.547 --> 16:48.887
<b><i>but we lost a great deal of our land.</i></b>

16:48.967 --> 16:50.387
<b>HOSHINA TERRITORY
PROVINCIAL OFFICIALS TERRITORY</b>

16:50.837 --> 16:54.307
<b>I don't like having to ask this,
but I'll be in your care, Yasaburo.</b>

16:54.387 --> 16:55.847
<b>HOSHINA TERRITORY</b>

16:55.937 --> 16:59.267
<b>Yeah. We fell for the enemy's strategy
and failed to finish off Kiyohara.</b>

17:00.027 --> 17:02.317
<b>The responsibility for this lies with me.</b>

17:03.277 --> 17:05.487
<b>The Hoshina party will provide
for the Shinomiya party's needs</b>

17:05.567 --> 17:06.907
<b>and perform rites for the fallen.</b>

17:06.987 --> 17:09.027
<b>Leave everything to us.</b>

17:09.737 --> 17:10.827
<b>I'm in your debt.</b>

17:10.907 --> 17:13.747
<b>With Lord Shinomiya on our side,
we have the strength of a hundred men!</b>

17:13.827 --> 17:16.457
<b>Next time, we'll slaughter them!</b>

17:16.537 --> 17:17.747
<b>Yeah…</b>

17:18.627 --> 17:21.547
<b><i>They're always way more fired up than us…</i></b>

17:22.167 --> 17:24.627
<b>MOSTLY THE GENTLE TYPE</b>

17:28.007 --> 17:32.847
<b>We could even merge our two parties
for the future.</b>

17:35.727 --> 17:37.017
<b>That might not be a bad idea.</b>

17:38.017 --> 17:41.277
<b>I heard that Suwa Myojin will surely rise.</b>

17:42.067 --> 17:45.357
<b>If it means living to see that day…
I'll do whatever it takes.</b>

17:46.487 --> 17:52.037
<b><i>Labeled enemies of the Imperial Court
and defeated in battle,</i></b>

17:52.117 --> 17:56.037
<b><i>the Suwa Sect will lose
all their lands if this continues.</i></b>

17:56.117 --> 17:58.877
<b><i>They had no choice but to stake everything
on a great upheaval.</i></b>

17:59.587 --> 18:03.917
<b><i>That awareness and resolve
gradually spread among them.</i></b>

18:36.457 --> 18:39.827
<b><i>Chief Chamberlain, Mitsunori of Minamoto.</i></b>

18:40.707 --> 18:43.457
<b><i>Imperial Councillor,
Noritaka of Tachibana.</i></b>

18:44.457 --> 18:48.087
<b><i>Provisional Middle Councillor,
Kinhira of Fujiwara.</i></b>

18:50.047 --> 18:53.387
<b><i>Those are all the promotions
for this occasion.</i></b>

18:56.267 --> 18:57.557
<b><i>It is a cruel thing</i></b>

18:57.637 --> 19:02.397
<b><i>when even talent cannot advance you
further because of your lineage.</i></b>

19:02.937 --> 19:05.357
<b><i>It is painful when your path
to advancement is blocked,</i></b>

19:06.187 --> 19:10.407
<b><i>but it is just as sad that you cannot rise
in rank without going to Kamakura.</i></b>

19:12.117 --> 19:16.827
<b><i>Mr. Kiyohara, there's no use lamenting
the advancement you'll never attain.</i></b>

19:16.907 --> 19:20.577
<b><i>We have no choice but to accept
that these are the times we live in.</i></b>

19:22.077 --> 19:28.377
<b><i>Even so, I'll wait for the day when
even those without noble lineage can rise.</i></b>

19:47.857 --> 19:50.527
<b>SUWA GRAND SHRINE</b>

19:50.607 --> 19:54.027
<b>Yoritsugu! Yoritsugu!</b>

19:54.907 --> 19:57.117
<b>Where is he?</b>

19:58.447 --> 19:59.957
<b>Yoritsugu!</b>

20:03.917 --> 20:07.547
<b>It's hard to report a defeat.</b>

20:11.337 --> 20:15.347
<b>More than anything, Lord Yorishige
will be overjoyed that you're safe.</b>

20:16.507 --> 20:17.717
<b>Look over there.</b>

20:18.927 --> 20:22.267
<b>Lord Yorishige had a hut built over there</b>

20:22.347 --> 20:24.477
<b>for times when
you would be on the battlefield.</b>

20:24.557 --> 20:27.187
<b>He allows no one inside,
performs ablution,</b>

20:27.267 --> 20:29.357
<b>and prays for your safe return.</b>

20:30.067 --> 20:31.237
<b>Ablution…</b>

20:32.487 --> 20:34.817
<b><i>To pour cold water over himself
at this time of year…</i></b>

20:35.617 --> 20:37.367
<b><i>He really cares that much about me…</i></b>

20:38.867 --> 20:40.827
<b><i>Now, I truly understand.</i></b>

20:41.577 --> 20:45.207
<b><i>My goal is the same as Mr. Yorishige's.</i></b>

20:46.167 --> 20:50.877
<b><i>To restore the Hojo
is to save the people of Shinano.</i></b>

20:51.837 --> 20:53.507
<b><i>This isn't the time to mope.</i></b>

20:54.337 --> 20:58.137
<b><i>I'm going to reclaim the throne
alongside him.</i></b>

20:59.637 --> 21:02.057
<b>I'm back, Mr. Yorishige.</b>

21:07.477 --> 21:08.687
<b><i>Yorishige</i></b>

21:10.067 --> 21:12.237
<b><i>is soaking in a hot spring.</i></b>

21:12.947 --> 21:15.487
<b><i>He's soaking in a hot spring
he unearthed with his holy power,</i></b>

21:16.197 --> 21:19.447
<b><i>with sake and snacks.</i></b>

21:19.987 --> 21:23.657
<b>We're risking our lives out there, and
you're off having the time of your life?</b>

21:23.747 --> 21:24.997
<b>You idiot Myojin!</b>

21:25.077 --> 21:28.167
<b>Well, I was performing ablution
until just a moment ago.</b>

21:28.247 --> 21:30.707
<b>Pouring hot water over yourself
just feels good!</b>

21:30.797 --> 21:32.047
<b>-It's fine!
-Hey!</b>

21:32.127 --> 21:34.627
<b>There's no rule
that says it has to be cold!</b>

21:35.127 --> 21:37.927
<b>Maybe I really can't work
with him after all.</b>

21:38.007 --> 21:39.967
<b>Teach him a lesson!</b>

21:41.467 --> 21:42.677
<b>Yeah.</b>

21:44.177 --> 21:50.107
<b><i>In this battle, the Suwa side lost land,
but gained stronger bonds.</i></b>

21:50.817 --> 21:56.107
<b><i>Above all, Tokiyuki and Yorishige
deepened their shared goal,</i></b>

21:56.197 --> 21:59.987
<b><i>and the Suwa side united
ahead of the coming great war…</i></b>

22:02.327 --> 22:03.537
<b><i>Or so it seemed.</i></b>

23:38.517 --> 23:39.837
<b><i>Let's go.</i></b>

23:38.967 --> 23:39.837
<b>EPISODE 18 (YEAR 1335):
THE BOY WHO BECAME A GOD</b>
